From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Nikolajs Agafonovs <nikolajs.agafonovs@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 14:50:23 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] Frosted glass for the tray and the menus

When the root window has _WALLPAPER_FROSTED_PMAP_ID (a screen-sized pixmap
of the wallpaper, blurred, tinted and capped in luminance, published by a
wallpaper program), the tray, its components and the menus cut their
backgrounds from it instead of filling them with their colours:
ClearTrayDrawable, the pager, the clock and the tray window itself, and
DrawMenu; DrawButton fills the inactive kinds (label, menu, tray, task,
minimized task) from it, so states stay solid (the active task, the active
desktop, the entry under the pointer, the pressed tray button).  Minimized
tasks are shown in brackets on the glass.  The components get their screen
position before Create (they draw there), and a change of the property
makes every tray take its new piece.  Without the property nothing
changes.
